# Trivy suppression list.
#
# Phase 7 (v3.10.13-18) emptied this file.  Prior to Phase 7 it carried 38
# per-CVE entries auditing Canonical's libssl1.1 focal backport state
# against Ubuntu's CVE JSON API (see Phase 4 v3.10.13-16 CHANGELOG entry
# for the audit script).  Phase 7 replaced the focal-security libssl1.1
# deb with Amazon Linux 2's openssl11-libs 1.1.1zg RPM (extracted into
# /usr/local/lib/ in the runtime stage; no dpkg metadata).  Since Trivy's
# OS-package scanner relies on dpkg/rpm package data to match CVE entries,
# the new libssl.so.1.1 + libcrypto.so.1.1 .so files don't trigger any
# package-level CVE matches at all, making the 38 audit entries obsolete.
#
# Phase 6 (v3.10.13-23) added 3 entries for Guava 14.0.1 CVEs, each
# justified by a JAR-bytecode reachability audit -- see docs/PHASE-6-AUDIT.md
# for the methodology + raw output, and docs/audit-guava-phase6.py for
# the script (re-runnable by future maintainers / CI).
#
# Format for new entries:
#   - one or two-line rationale comment block
#   - reference URL on its own line (NVD, Ubuntu CVE JSON,
#     explore.alas.aws.amazon.com, etc.)
#   - the bare CVE ID on its own line.

# -- Guava 14.0.1 residuals (Phase 6, v3.10.13-23) --------------------------
#
# guava-14.0.1.jar ships inside the UniFi Video bundle and is coupled to
# Guice 3.0's ABI (Guice 3.0 references com.google.common.collect.MapMaker
# internals removed in Guava 20+, so the .jar can't be bumped without
# simultaneously bumping Guice to 5.1.0; per docs/PHASE-5-ROADMAP.md
# that's a 3+ session bytecode-rewrite effort rated High risk).  Instead
# we audited reachability of the three vulnerable APIs across all 104
# shipped JARs (36,498 .class files) at the bytecode constant-pool level
# -- zero call sites found in any JAR other than guava-14.0.1.jar itself.
# Audit script: docs/audit-guava-phase6.py.  Evidence + per-set raw
# output: docs/PHASE-6-AUDIT.md.

# CVE-2023-2976 (medium) -- com.google.common.io.Files.createTempDir()
# creates temp dirs world-readable on POSIX, allowing local information
# disclosure.  Fixed in Guava 32.0.0-jre.  Audit: zero Methodref
# invocations of Files.createTempDir across all 104 shipped JARs.
# https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2023-2976
CVE-2023-2976

# CVE-2018-10237 (medium) -- AtomicDoubleArray (de)serialization and
# CompoundOrdering allow unbounded memory allocation from attacker-
# controlled input.  Fixed in Guava 24.1.1-jre.  Audit: zero Class
# references to AtomicDoubleArray or CompoundOrdering, zero Methodref
# invocations of Ordering.compound (the only public entry to
# CompoundOrdering), and zero Utf8-string references to either FQN
# across all 104 shipped JARs.
# https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2018-10237
CVE-2018-10237

# CVE-2020-8908 (low) -- same Files.createTempDir() temp-dir permission
# issue as CVE-2023-2976, originally filed separately.  Fixed in
# Guava 30.0-jre.  Same audit verdict as CVE-2023-2976: zero reachable
# call sites.
# https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2020-8908
CVE-2020-8908

# -- end Guava 14.0.1 residuals ---------------------------------------------

# -- jackson-databind 2.12.7.2 PTV-bypass residuals (Phase 7, v3.10.13-24) --
#
# jackson-databind is pinned at 2.12.7.2 because Mongojack 2.7.0 calls a
# substantial set of jackson-databind INTERNAL APIs (BeanDeserializer,
# BeanSerializerBase, DefaultSerializerProvider, TokenBuffer,
# SettableBeanProperty, Annotated, etc.) whose ABI compatibility across the
# 2.12 -> 2.18/2.21/3.x jump has not been verified -- see CHANGELOG
# v3.10.13-10 for the Phase 2A empirical compatibility work that justified
# pinning at 2.12.7.2 in the first place, and the v3.10.13-12 / v3.10.13-17
# follow-ups that bump jackson-core in isolation instead (jackson-core's
# public API surface is stable across 2.x minors; jackson-databind's is
# not, given Mongojack's internal-API usage).
#
# CVE-2026-54512 and CVE-2026-54513 are both PolymorphicTypeValidator (PTV)
# bypasses: they are only reachable when an ObjectMapper has polymorphic
# typing enabled via `@JsonTypeInfo(use = Id.CLASS)` or `Id.MINIMAL_CLASS`
# (or the equivalent `enableDefaultTyping()`/`activateDefaultTyping()` global
# toggle) AND a PolymorphicTypeValidator is configured to gate it. Audited
# both airvision's and Mongojack 2.7.0's decompiled sources for all three
# preconditions -- zero hits. Audit script: docs/audit-jackson-ptv-phase7.py.
#
# airvision's only two `@JsonTypeInfo` usages (Event.java, UserGroup.java)
# use `Id.NAME` with an explicit `@JsonSubTypes` allowlist of logical type
# names -- a different, non-PTV-gated resolution path that never calls
# DatabindContext._resolveAndValidateGeneric() or
# BasicPolymorphicTypeValidator.Builder.allowIfSubTypeIsArray() (the two
# vulnerable methods) at all. No ObjectMapper construction site in either
# airvision or Mongojack calls enableDefaultTyping/activateDefaultTyping,
# and MongoJackModule.configure() only registers BSON type serializers/
# deserializers (ObjectId, DBRef, etc.) -- no polymorphic typing, no PTV.

# CVE-2026-54512 (high, CVSS 8.1 AV:N/AC:H) -- PolymorphicTypeValidator
# bypass via generic type parameters (e.g. java.util.ArrayList<Evil>
# smuggles Evil past an ArrayList-only allowlist). Requires Id.CLASS/
# Id.MINIMAL_CLASS polymorphic typing + a configured PTV -- neither present
# anywhere in airvision or Mongojack 2.7.0. Fixed in 2.18.8 / 2.21.4 / 3.1.4.
# https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-j3rv-43j4-c7qm
CVE-2026-54512

# CVE-2026-54513 (high, CVSS 8.1 AV:N/AC:H) -- PolymorphicTypeValidator
# bypass via array component type (BasicPolymorphicTypeValidator.Builder.
# allowIfSubTypeIsArray() allowlists any array by clazz.isArray() without
# checking the element type). Same precondition and same audit verdict as
# CVE-2026-54512: zero reachable trigger. Fixed in 2.18.8 / 2.21.4 / 3.1.4.
# https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-54513
CVE-2026-54513

# -- end jackson-databind 2.12.7.2 PTV-bypass residuals ---------------------
#
# If a future change adds polymorphic typing (Id.CLASS/Id.MINIMAL_CLASS) or
# a PolymorphicTypeValidator anywhere in airvision or a dependency, re-run
# docs/audit-jackson-ptv-phase7.py; a non-zero exit means these two
# suppressions must be reconsidered (and likely means jackson-databind needs
# the full Phase-2A-style compatibility bump instead).
#
# If a future change reintroduces a manually-installed deb/rpm in the
# runtime image and Trivy starts reporting false positives, add new
# entries here with the per-CVE Ubuntu-CVE-JSON or
# explore.alas.aws.amazon.com reference URL above the entry.  See
# the v3.10.13-16 CHANGELOG for the audit methodology.
